  "verbalization": "Azadiradionolide is consistently linked to the Raji cell line through multiple pathways, with SNU-387 serving as a common intermediate in all three evidence chains. The drug's interaction with SNU-387, which is targeted by three distinct compounds—10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one, (2-Methyl-5-Prop-1-En-2-Ylcyclohex-2-En-1-Yl) Acetate, and 2-(hydroxymethyl)-3-[(E)-prop-1-enyl]phenol—suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of a complex metabolic or signaling pathway. The recurring involvement of SNU-387 and its downstream targets implies that Azadiradionolide may act through a mechanism that affects the expression or activity of these compounds, possibly by interfering with a shared biological process. The evidence supports a plausible mechanistic link between Azadiradionolide and Raji cells, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
